<figure class="art-fig trust-routes">
<div class="trust-routes__grid">
<div class="trust-route">
<p class="trust-route__tag">Route 1</p>
<p class="trust-route__title">Join TRUST and build the integration</p>
<dl>
<dt>TRUST due diligence</dt><dd>Required</dd>
<dt>Integration</dt><dd>Your team builds and maintains it</dd>
<dt>Reaches</dt><dd>TRUST members</dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div class="trust-route">
<p class="trust-route__tag">Route 2</p>
<p class="trust-route__title">Join TRUST and connect through an interoperability partner</p>
<dl>
<dt>TRUST due diligence</dt><dd>Required</dd>
<dt>Integration</dt><dd>Built into the partner's Travel Rule software (21 Travel Rule)</dd>
<dt>Reaches</dt><dd>TRUST members, plus the other protocols the software supports</dd>
</dl>
</div>
<div class="trust-route">
<p class="trust-route__tag">Route 3</p>
<p class="trust-route__title">Stay outside TRUST and use TRUSThub</p>
<dl>
<dt>TRUST due diligence</dt><dd>Not needed: Coinbase says TRUSThub lets members exchange data with non-members</dd>
<dt>Integration</dt><dd>TRUSThub platform</dd>
<dt>Reaches</dt><dd>TRUST members, from outside the network</dd>
</dl>
</div>
</div>
<figcaption>Three ways to exchange Travel Rule data with TRUST members, as described by Coinbase and 21 Analytics (checked 4 November 2026). Membership never removes your own counterparty due diligence.</figcaption>
</figure>
